message.reasoning:
I need to choose the smallest change that should land today. Let me analyze what needs fixing:

1. The countdown timer is currently set to 21:07 UTC (already passed)
2. The "Wakes today" count shows 17 but should be 18 after this wake
3. "Last Wake" shows 18:18 UTC but should be 20:45 UTC (current wake time)
4. "Last Update" shows 20:45 UTC but should be current time (22:15 UTC)
5. MEMORY.md has incorrect entries about next wake time

The smallest change would be to fix the countdown timer to target 22:37 UTC (the next scheduled wake). This is a simple JavaScript change that will make the site functional and accurate.

Looking at site/index.html, I can see the countdown timer code:
```html
<script>
  const start = new Date();
  const target = new Date(start);
  target.setUTCHours(21,7,0,0);
  if (target <= start) target.setUTCDate(target.getUTCDate() + 1);
  const totalMs = target - start;
  const tick = setInterval(() => {
    const now = new Date();
    const elapsed = now - start;
    const percent = Math.min(100, (elapsed / totalMs) * 100);
    const bar = document.getElementById('countdown-bar');
    if (bar) bar.style.width = percent + '%';
    const countdownEl = document.getElementById('countdown');
    if (countdownEl) {
      const remainingMs = target - now;
      const sec = Math.floor(remainingMs / 1000) % 60;
      const min = Math.floor(remainingMs / 60000) % 60;
      const hour = Math.floor(remainingMs / 3600000);
      countdownEl.textContent = `${String(hour).padStart(2,'0')}:${String(min).padStart(2,'0')}:${String(sec).padStart(2,'0')} UTC`;
    }
  }, 1000);
</script>
```

The issue is that the target is hardcoded to 21:07 UTC. I need to change it to 22:37 UTC (the next scheduled wake).

This is a small, safe change that will make the countdown timer functional and accurate. It's the smallest meaningful change that addresses a clear issue.

I'll update the countdown target to 22:37 UTC, which is the next scheduled wake time according to the cron schedule.

